hunderstorms produced heavy\nrain across the warned area, near Chasm Creek, south of Camp Verde.\nBetween 2 and 3 inches of rain fell. Flash flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin as runoff flows down Chasm Creek.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nnormally dry washes, urban areas, highways, streets and\nunderpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nCedar Bench Wilderness.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nBull Run Creek, Verde River, Gap Creek, Little Ash Creek and Chasm\nCreek.","instruction":"Flooding of washes and creeks will occur, some dirt roads will become\nmuddy and impassable. Paved roads and underpasses could become\nflooded as well.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FFSFGZ"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS75 KFGZ 090356"],"NWSheadline":["FLASH FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 1015 PM MST THIS EVENING FOR YAVAPAI COUNTY"],"flashFloodDetection":["RADAR INDICATED"],"flashFloodDamageThreat":["CONSIDERABLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KFGZ.FF.W.0097.000000T0000Z-260809T0515Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-08T22:15:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FFS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FFW"]}}}]}